{"id":"mahabharata-7-133","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":133,"title":"त्रयस्त्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 133 · Karna and Kripa quarrel","summary":{"en":"As the Pandava army surges, Karna boasts of what he will do, and Kripa tells him to stop talking and fight, since he has been routed again and again by Arjuna. Karna replies that heroes who boast should still strike.","kn":"ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಉಕ್ಕುತ್ತಿರಲು ಕರ್ಣ ತಾನು ಮಾಡುವುದನ್ನು ಜಂಬ ಕೊಚ್ಚುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಂದ ಮತ್ತೆ ಮತ್ತೆ ಸೋತಿರುವುದರಿಂದ ಮಾತು ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಹೋರಾಡೆಂದು ಕೃಪ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಜಂಬ ಕೊಚ್ಚುವ ವೀರರೂ ಹೊಡೆಯಬೇಕೆಂದು ಕರ್ಣ ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"पाण्डव सेना उमड़ने पर कर्ण अपने कार्यों की डींग हाँकता है, और कृप कहते हैं कि बातें छोड़कर लड़ो, क्योंकि अर्जुन ने तुम्हें बार-बार हराया है। कर्ण उत्तर देता है कि डींग हाँकने वाले वीरों को भी प्रहार करना चाहिए।","te":"పాండవసేన ఉప్పొంగుతుండగా కర్ణుడు తాను చేయబోయేదాని గురించి గొప్పలు చెబుతాడు; అర్జునుని చేతిలో మళ్లీ మళ్లీ ఓడావు కాబట్టి మాటలు మాని పోరాడమని కృపుడు అంటాడు. గొప్పలు చెప్పే వీరులు కూడా కొట్టాలని కర్ణుడు బదులిస్తాడు.","ta":"பாண்டவப் படை பொங்க, கர்ணன் தான் செய்யப்போவதைப் பற்றிப் பெருமை பேச, அர்ஜுனனிடம் மீண்டும் மீண்டும் தோற்றதால் பேச்சை விட்டுப் போரிடு என்று கிருபர் கூறுகிறார். பெருமை பேசும் வீரரும் தாக்க வேண்டும் என்று கர்ணன் பதிலளிக்கிறான்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡവ സേന ഇരച്ചുകയറുമ്പോൾ കർണ്ണൻ താൻ എന്ത് ചെയ്യുമെന്ന് വീമ്പു പറയുന്നു; അർജുനനാൽ ആവർത്തിച്ച് തോൽപ്പിക്കപ്പെട്ടതിനാൽ സംസാരം നിർത്തി പൊരുതാൻ കൃപർ പറയുന്നു. വീമ്പിളക്കുന്ന വീരന്മാരും പ്രഹരിക്കണമെന്ന് കർണ്ണൻ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.133; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"उदीर्यमाणं तद्दृष्ट्वा पाण्डवानां महद्बलम् ।\nअविषह्यं च मन्वानः कर्णं दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the great Pandava army surging up, and thinking it unbearable, Duryodhana spoke to Karna."}},{"n":2,"text":"अयं स कालः संप्राप्तो मित्राणां मित्रवत्सल ।\nत्रायस्व समरे कर्ण सर्वान्योधान्महाबल ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is the time that has come, Karna, you who are kind to your friends. Protect all the warriors in battle, mighty one."}},{"n":3,"text":"पाञ्चालैर्मत्स्यकैकेयैः पाण्डवैश्च महारथैः ।\nवृतान्समन्तात्संक्रुद्धैर्निःश्वसद्भिरिवोरगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are surrounded on every side by Panchalas, Matsyas, Kekayas and the great chariot-fighters of the Pandavas, angry and hissing like serpents."}},{"n":4,"text":"एते नदन्ति संहृष्टाः पाण्डवा जितकाशिनः ।\nशक्रोपमाश्च बहवः पाञ्चालानां रथव्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These Pandavas, in joy and flushed with victory, roar, and so do the many hosts of Panchala chariots, equal to Indra.\""}},{"text":"कर्ण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Karna said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"परित्रातुमिह प्राप्तो यदि पार्थं पुरंदरः ।\nतमप्याशु पराजित्य ततो हन्तास्मि पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Even if Indra has come here to protect Partha, I shall quickly defeat him as well and then kill the Pandava."}},{"n":6,"text":"सत्यं ते प्रतिजानामि समाश्वसिहि भारत ।\nहन्तास्मि पाण्डुतनयान्पाञ्चालांश्च समागतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I promise you truly, Bharata; be comforted. I shall kill the sons of Pandu and the Panchalas who have come together."}},{"n":7,"text":"जयं ते प्रतिजानामि वासवस्येव पावकिः ।\nप्रियं तव मया कार्यमिति जीवामि पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"I promise you victory, as Fire's son promised Indra; I live, king, to do what pleases you."}},{"n":8,"text":"सर्वेषामेव पार्थानां फल्गुनो बलवत्तरः ।\nतस्यामोघां विमोक्ष्यामि शक्तिं शक्रविनिर्मिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Of all the Parthas Phalguna is the strongest; I shall loose at him the unfailing spear made by Indra."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्मिन्हते महेष्वासे भ्रातरस्तस्य मानद ।\nतव वश्या भविष्यन्ति वनं यास्यन्ति वा पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that great bowman is killed, honorable man, his brothers will come under your control or go again to the forest."}},{"n":10,"text":"मयि जीवति कौरव्य विषादं मा कृथाः क्वचित् ।\nअहं जेष्यामि समरे सहितान्सर्वपाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While I live, descendant of Kuru, never be downcast. I shall conquer all the Pandavas together in battle."}},{"n":11,"text":"पाञ्चालान्केकयांश्चैव वृष्णींश्चापि समागतान् ।\nबाणौघैः शकलीकृत्य तव दास्यामि मेदिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"After splintering the Panchalas, Kekayas and the Vrishnis who have gathered with floods of arrows, I shall give you the earth.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"एवं ब्रुवाणं कर्णं तु कृपः शारद्वतोऽब्रवीत् ।\nस्मयन्निव महाबाहुः सूतपुत्रमिदं वचः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Karna spoke so, Kripa son of Sharadvat, mighty-armed, as if smiling, said this to the charioteer's son."}},{"n":13,"text":"शोभनं शोभनं कर्ण सनाथः कुरुपुंगवः ।\nत्वया नाथेन राधेय वचसा यदि सिध्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Well said, well said, Karna! The Kuru bull has a protector in you, Radheya, if success comes by words."}},{"n":14,"text":"बहुशः कत्थसे कर्ण कौरव्यस्य समीपतः ।\nन तु ते विक्रमः कश्चिद्दृश्यते बलमेव वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"You boast often, Karna, near the Kaurava, but no valor or strength of yours is seen."}},{"n":15,"text":"समागमः पाण्डुसुतैर्दृष्टस्ते बहुशो युधि ।\nसर्वत्र निर्जितश्चासि पाण्डवैः सूतनन्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have often met the sons of Pandu in battle, and everywhere you were beaten by the Pandavas, joy of the charioteers."}},{"n":16,"text":"ह्रियमाणे तदा कर्ण गन्धर्वैर्धृतराष्ट्रजे ।\nतदायुध्यन्त सैन्यानि त्वमेकस्तु पलायथाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Dhritarashtra's son was being carried off by gandharvas, the armies fought, but you alone fled."}},{"n":17,"text":"विराटनगरे चापि समेताः सर्वकौरवाः ।\nपार्थेन निर्जिता युद्धे त्वं च कर्ण सहानुजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And at Virata's city, when all the Kauravas gathered, they were beaten by Partha, and you too, Karna, with your younger brother."}},{"n":18,"text":"एकस्याप्यसमर्थस्त्वं फल्गुनस्य रणाजिरे ।\nकथमुत्सहसे जेतुं सकृष्णान्सर्वपाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You cannot match even Phalguna alone on the field. How can you hope to conquer all the Pandavas with Krishna?"}},{"n":19,"text":"अब्रुवन्कर्ण युध्यस्व बहु कत्थसि सूतज ।\nअनुक्त्वा विक्रमेद्यस्तु तद्वै सत्पुरुषव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fight without talking, Karna; you boast a great deal, son of a charioteer. He who acts valiantly without having spoken, that is the way of good men."}},{"n":20,"text":"गर्जित्वा सूतपुत्र त्वं शारदाभ्रमिवाजलम् ।\nनिष्फलो दृश्यसे कर्ण तच्च राजा न बुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"You thunder, charioteer's son, like an autumn cloud without water; you look fruitless, Karna, and the king does not understand this."}},{"n":21,"text":"तावद्गर्जसि राधेय यावत्पार्थं न पश्यसि ।\nपुरा पार्थं हि ते दृष्ट्वा दुर्लभं गर्जितं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You thunder only so long, Radheya, as you do not see Partha. Once you have seen Partha, your thunder will become rare."}},{"n":22,"text":"त्वमनासाद्य तान्बाणान्फल्गुनस्य विगर्जसि ।\nपार्थसायकविद्धस्य दुर्लभं गर्जितं भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You thunder without having met Phalguna's arrows; when pierced by Partha's arrows, your thunder will become rare."}},{"n":23,"text":"बाहुभिः क्षत्रियाः शूरा वाग्भिः शूरा द्विजातयः ।\nधनुषा फल्गुनः शूरः कर्णः शूरो मनोरथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warriors are brave by their arms, Brahmins by their words, Phalguna by his bow, and Karna by his wishes.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"एवं परुषितस्तेन तदा शारद्वतेन सः ।\nकर्णः प्रहरतां श्रेष्ठः कृपं वाक्यमथाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus harshly spoken to by Sharadvat's son, Karna, best of those who strike, answered Kripa."}},{"n":25,"text":"शूरा गर्जन्ति सततं प्रावृषीव बलाहकाः ।\nफलं चाशु प्रयच्छन्ति बीजमुप्तमृताविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Brave men always thunder, like clouds in the rains, and give fruit quickly, like a seed sown in its season."}},{"n":26,"text":"दोषमत्र न पश्यामि शूराणां रणमूर्धनि ।\nतत्तद्विकत्थमानानां भारं चोद्वहतां मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I see no fault here in heroes at the head of battle who boast this way and that and carry the burden in the fight."}},{"n":27,"text":"यं भारं पुरुषो वोढुं मनसा हि व्यवस्यति ।\nदैवमस्य ध्रुवं तत्र साहाय्यायोपपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever burden a man resolves in his mind to bear, fate surely comes there to help him."}},{"n":28,"text":"व्यवसायद्वितीयोऽहं मनसा भारमुद्वहन् ।\nगर्जामि यद्यहं विप्र तव किं तत्र नश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"With resolve as my second, I bear the burden in my mind. If I thunder, Brahmin, what of yours is lost by it?"}},{"n":29,"text":"वृथा शूरा न गर्जन्ति सजला इव तोयदाः ।\nसामर्थ्यमात्मनो ज्ञात्वा ततो गर्जन्ति पण्डिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Heroes do not thunder in vain, like clouds with water. Knowing their own ability, the wise thunder."}},{"n":30,"text":"सोऽहमद्य रणे यत्तः सहितौ कृष्णपाण्डवौ ।\nउत्सहे तरसा जेतुं ततो गर्जामि गौतम ॥","meaning":{"en":"So today, ready in battle, I can conquer with force Krishna and the Pandava together; therefore I thunder, Gautama."}},{"n":31,"text":"पश्य त्वं गर्जितस्यास्य फलं मे विप्र सानुगः ।\nहत्वा पाण्डुसुतानाजौ सहकृष्णान्ससात्वतान् ।\nदुर्योधनाय दास्यामि पृथिवीं हतकण्टकाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See, Brahmin, with your followers, the fruit of this thundering of mine: having killed the sons of Pandu with Krishna and the Satvatas in battle, I shall give Duryodhana the earth with its thorns removed.\""}},{"text":"कृप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kripa said:"}},{"n":32,"text":"मनोरथप्रलापो मे न ग्राह्यस्तव सूतज ।\nयदा क्षिपसि वै कृष्णौ धर्मराजं च पाण्डवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I do not accept what you say, charioteer's son, as only the babble of wishes, when you insult the two Krishnas and the Pandava, king of dharma."}},{"n":33,"text":"ध्रुवस्तत्र जयः कर्ण यत्र युद्धविशारदौ ।\nदेवगन्धर्वयक्षाणां मनुष्योरगरक्षसाम् ।\nदंशितानामपि रणे अजेयौ कृष्णपाण्डवौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Victory is certain where those two skilled in war are, Karna; Krishna and Pandava cannot be conquered in battle even by gods, gandharvas, yakshas, men, serpents and rakshasas, though armored."}},{"n":34,"text":"ब्रह्मण्यः सत्यवाग्दान्तो गुरुदैवतपूजकः ।\nनित्यं धर्मरतश्चैव कृतास्त्रश्च विशेषतः ।\nधृतिमांश्च कृतज्ञश्च धर्मपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, son of Dharma, is devoted to Brahmins, truthful, self-controlled, a worshipper of teachers and gods, always devoted to dharma, especially skilled in weapons, steady and grateful."}},{"n":35,"text":"भ्रातरश्चास्य बलिनः सर्वास्त्रेषु कृतश्रमाः ।\nगुरुवृत्तिरताः प्राज्ञा धर्मनित्या यशस्विनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And his brothers are strong, trained in all weapons, devoted to serving elders, wise, ever righteous and renowned."}},{"n":36,"text":"संबन्धिनश्चेन्द्रवीर्याः स्वनुरक्ताः प्रहारिणः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नः शिखण्डी च दौर्मुखिर्जनमेजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His in-laws, with Indra's valor, very devoted, striking: Dhrishtadyumna, Shikhandi, Draupadi's sons, Janamejaya son of Durmukha,"}},{"n":37,"text":"चन्द्रसेनो भद्रसेनः कीर्तिधर्मा ध्रुवो धरः ।\nवसुचन्द्रो दामचन्द्रः सिंहचन्द्रः सुवेधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chandrasena, Bhadrasena, Kirtidharman, Dhruva, Dhara, Vasuchandra, Damachandra, Simhachandra and Suvedhana,"}},{"n":38,"text":"द्रुपदस्य तथा पुत्रा द्रुपदश्च महास्त्रवित् ।\nयेषामर्थाय संयत्तो मत्स्यराजः सहानुगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drupada's sons, and Drupada himself, a master of great weapons, and the king of Matsya with his followers, who fights for their sake,"}},{"n":39,"text":"शतानीकः सुदशनः श्रुतानीकः श्रुतध्वजः ।\nबलानीको जयानीको जयाश्वो रथवाहनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shatanika, Sudarshana, Shrutanika, Shrutadhvaja, Balanika, Jayanika, Jayashva, Rathavahana,"}},{"n":40,"text":"चन्द्रोदयः कामरथो विराटभ्रातरः शुभाः ।\nयमौ च द्रौपदेयाश्च राक्षसश्च घटोत्कचः ।\nयेषामर्थाय युध्यन्ते न तेषां विद्यते क्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chandrodaya, Kamaratha, the fine brothers of Virata, the twins, Draupadi's sons and the rakshasa Ghatotkacha. Those for whom they fight have no destruction."}},{"n":41,"text":"कामं खलु जगत्सर्वं सदेवासुरमानवम् ।\nसयक्षराक्षसगणं सभूतभुजगद्विपम् ।\nनिःशेषमस्त्रवीर्येण कुर्यातां भीमफल्गुनौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima and Phalguna could, if they wished, with the power of their weapons make the whole world, with gods, asuras and men, with yakshas and rakshasas, with spirits, serpents and elephants, utterly empty."}},{"n":42,"text":"युधिष्ठिरश्च पृथिवीं निर्दहेद्घोरचक्षुषा ।\nअप्रमेयबलः शौरिर्येषामर्थे च दंशितः ।\nकथं तान्संयुगे कर्ण जेतुमुत्सहसे परान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Yudhishthira could burn the earth with his terrible glance. And Shauri of immeasurable strength is armored for their sake. How can you hope to conquer those enemies in battle, Karna?"}},{"n":43,"text":"महानपनयस्त्वेष तव नित्यं हि सूतज ।\nयस्त्वमुत्सहसे योद्धुं समरे शौरिणा सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is always your great mistake, charioteer's son, that you dare to fight with Shauri in battle.\""}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":44,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु राधेयः प्रहसन्भरतर्षभ ।\nअब्रवीच्च तदा कर्णो गुरुं शारद्वतं कृपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed thus, Radheya, laughing, O best of Bharatas, said to his teacher Kripa son of Sharadvat."}},{"n":45,"text":"सत्यमुक्तं त्वया ब्रह्मन्पाण्डवान्प्रति यद्वचः ।\nएते चान्ये च बहवो गुणाः पाण्डुसुतेषु वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You have spoken the truth, Brahmin, in what you say about the Pandavas. These and many other virtues are in the sons of Pandu."}},{"n":46,"text":"अजय्याश्च रणे पार्था देवैरपि सवासवैः ।\nसदैत्ययक्षगन्धर्वपिशाचोरगराक्षसैः ।\nतथापि पार्थाञ्जेष्यामि शक्त्या वासवदत्तया ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Parthas cannot be conquered in battle even by gods with Indra, with daityas, yakshas, gandharvas, pishachas, serpents and rakshasas; yet I shall conquer them with the spear given by Indra."}},{"n":47,"text":"ममाप्यमोघा दत्तेयं शक्तिः शक्रेण वै द्विज ।\nएतया निहनिष्यामि सव्यसाचिनमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"This unfailing spear was given to me too, Brahmin, by Shakra; with it I shall kill Savyasachin in battle."}},{"n":48,"text":"हते तु पाण्डवे कृष्णो भ्रातरश्चास्य सोदराः ।\nअनर्जुना न शक्ष्यन्ति महीं भोक्तुं कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the Pandava is killed, Krishna and his own brothers, without Arjuna, will not be able to enjoy the earth in any way."}},{"n":49,"text":"तेषु नष्टेषु सर्वेषु पृथिवीयं ससागरा ।\nअयत्नात्कौरवेयस्य वशे स्थास्यति गौतम ॥","meaning":{"en":"When they are all lost, this earth with its oceans will come under the Kaurava's control without effort, Gautama."}},{"n":50,"text":"सुनीतैरिह सर्वार्थाः सिध्यन्ते नात्र संशयः ।\nएतमर्थमहं ज्ञात्वा ततो गर्जामि गौतम ॥","meaning":{"en":"By sound policy all ends are surely achieved; knowing this, I thunder, Gautama."}},{"n":51,"text":"त्वं तु वृद्धश्च विप्रश्च अशक्तश्चापि संयुगे ।\nकृतस्नेहश्च पार्थेषु मोहान्मामवमन्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But you are old, a Brahmin, powerless in battle and fond of the Parthas, and out of delusion you disrespect me."}},{"n":52,"text":"यद्येवं वक्ष्यसे भूयो मामप्रियमिह द्विज ।\nततस्ते खड्गमुद्यम्य जिह्वां छेत्स्यामि दुर्मते ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you say again anything displeasing to me, Brahmin, I shall raise my sword and cut out your tongue, fool."}},{"n":53,"text":"यच्चापि पाण्डवान्विप्र स्तोतुमिच्छसि संयुगे ।\nभीषयन्सर्वसैन्यानि कौरवेयाणि दुर्मते ।\nअत्रापि शृणु मे वाक्यं यथावद्गदतो द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"And that you wish to praise the Pandavas in battle, frightening all the Kaurava armies, fool, hear my answer to this too, Brahmin, as I say it truly."}},{"n":54,"text":"दुर्योधनश्च द्रोणश्च शकुनिर्दुर्मुखो जयः ।\nदुःशासनो वृषसेनो मद्रराजस्त्वमेव च ।\nसोमदत्तश्च भूरिश्च तथा द्रौणिर्विविंशतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, Drona, Shakuni, Durmukha, Jaya, Duhshasana, Vrishasena, the king of Madra, you yourself, Somadatta, Bhuri, Drona's son and Vivimshati:"}},{"n":55,"text":"तिष्ठेयुर्दंशिता यत्र सर्वे युद्धविशारदाः ।\nजयेदेतान्रणे को नु शक्रतुल्यबलोऽप्यरिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"if all these skilled in war stood in armor, what enemy, even if equal to Shakra in strength, could defeat them in battle?"}},{"n":56,"text":"शूराश्च हि कृतास्त्राश्च बलिनः स्वर्गलिप्सवः ।\nधर्मज्ञा युद्धकुशला हन्युर्युद्धे सुरानपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brave, trained in weapons, strong, desiring heaven, knowing dharma, skilled in war, they could kill even gods in battle."}},{"n":57,"text":"एते स्थास्यन्ति संग्रामे पाण्डवानां वधार्थिनः ।\nजयमाकाङ्क्षमाणा हि कौरवेयस्य दंशिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"These will stand in the fight, desiring to kill the Pandavas, armored and wishing victory for the Kaurava."}},{"n":58,"text":"दैवायत्तमहं मन्ये जयं सुबलिनामपि ।\nयत्र भीष्मो महाबाहुः शेते शरशताचितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think the victory of even the very strong depends on fate, since the mighty-armed Bhishma lies pierced by hundreds of arrows."}},{"n":59,"text":"विकर्णश्चित्रसेनश्च बाह्लीकोऽथ जयद्रथः ।\nभूरिश्रवा जयश्चैव जलसंधः सुदक्षिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Vikarna, Chitrasena, Bahlika, Jayadratha, Bhurishravas, Jaya, Jalasandha, Sudakshina,"}},{"n":60,"text":"शलश्च रथिनां श्रेष्ठो भगदत्तश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nएते चान्ये च राजानो देवैरपि सुदुर्जयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shala, best of chariot-fighters, and mighty Bhagadatta, and these and other kings hard to conquer even for the gods,"}},{"n":61,"text":"निहताः समरे शूराः पाण्डवैर्बलवत्तराः ।\nकिमन्यद्दैवसंयोगान्मन्यसे पुरुषाधम ॥","meaning":{"en":"brave men who were stronger than the Pandavas were killed in battle; what else do you take that to be but the working of fate, lowest of men?"}},{"n":62,"text":"यांश्च तान्स्तौषि सततं दुर्योधनरिपून्द्विज ।\nतेषामपि हताः शूराः शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And those whom you always praise, Brahmin, enemies of Duryodhana, among them too heroes have been killed by hundreds and thousands."}},{"n":63,"text":"क्षीयन्ते सर्वसैन्यानि कुरूणां पाण्डवैः सह ।\nप्रभावं नात्र पश्यामि पाण्डवानां कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the armies of the Kurus and the Pandavas are dwindling; I see no power of the Pandavas in this at all."}},{"n":64,"text":"यांस्तान्बलवतो नित्यं मन्यसे त्वं द्विजाधम ।\nयतिष्येऽहं यथाशक्ति योद्धुं तैः सह संयुगे ।\nदुर्योधनहितार्थाय जयो दैवे प्रतिष्ठितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those you always think strong, lowest of Brahmins, with them I shall try to fight in battle as best I can, for Duryodhana's good; victory rests with fate.\""}}]}]}